<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Frederick III of Denmark</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">1609–1670</span></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Frederick III was king of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/denmark">Denmark</a> and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/norway">Norway</a> from 1648 to 1670. His war with <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/sweden">Sweden</a> cost Denmark <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/scania">Scania</a> and its other provinces east of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/oresund">the Sound</a> in 1658, but he won fame defending <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/copenhagen">Copenhagen</a> during the Swedish siege. In 1660 he used the crisis to make the monarchy hereditary and absolute, set down in the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/kings-law">King's Law</a> of 1665.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/frederick-iii-of-denmark.jpg" alt="Frederick III of Denmark" width="320" height="404" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Paul Prieur · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Frederik_III,_1663.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
